#!/bin/sh
# A local convenience, not the gate. CI is the gate: `check.yml` runs the
# every-change check on the pull request and again on main (issue #123), so this
# hook does not repeat it — a landing used to pay the same suite twice.
#
# Install once per clone: `just hooks` (git config core.hooksPath .githooks).
#
# Issue #141: refuse a push to main here to name the remedy locally, because
# GitHub's own refusal names none. `--no-verify` skips this and loses only the
# message: the server-side `main-protection` ruleset refuses the push anyway
# (no force-push, no delete, green `check`, and a pull request is required).
#
# stdin is one line per ref:
#   <local ref> <local sha> <remote ref> <remote sha>
set -e
while read -r _local_ref _local_sha remote_ref _remote_sha; do
    case "$remote_ref" in
        refs/heads/main)
            echo "main is protected; use \`just land\` (push the task branch, PR, merge)." >&2
            exit 1
            ;;
    esac
done
exit 0
